0014: def main(input_grid):
0015:     """
0016:     Move each non-distractor puzzle piece into the matching black hole inside a gray object.
0017: 
0018:     Input structure:
0019:     - Gray rectangular objects contain black interior holes.
0020:     - Colored objects outside the rectangles may match those hole shapes.
0021:     - Distractor objects share the most common non-gray object color.
0022: 
0023:     Rule:
0024:     - Extract gray objects and their black interior masks.
0025:     - Treat the most common non-gray object color as the distractor color.
0026:     - For every other colored sprite, compare its mask to each hole mask and paste exact matches into the hole.
0027: 
0028:     Key insight:
0029:     - Fit is determined by binary shape equality, not by the piece color or its original position.
0030:     """
0031:     # Plan:
0032:     # 1. Parse the input into objects, sprites, and black holes inside the grey objects
0033:     # 2. Identify color of distracter objects.
0034:     # 3. Turn each object into a sprite
